Here's how you’d implement that in Java:

```java
import java.util.List;

public class BreadSearch {
    public static boolean containsItem(List<String> list, String item) {
        for (String loaf : list) {
            if (loaf.equals(item)) {
                return true; // Found the perfect loaf!
            }
        }
        return false; // The loaf is missing from the batch.
    }
}
```

This function kneads through the list one element at a time, checking for equality with your target string. If it finds a match, it immediately recognizes the loaf and returns true; if it reaches the end without finding the loaf, it returns false, indicating the batch doesn’t contain the item.

